<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index gains 0.65 pct.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index gains 0.65 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index rose 0.46 points, 0.65 percent, to 69.78 points on Friday after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index rose 18.88 points to 3,110.90.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 10.49 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
